From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:20:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] eip155: require exactly the required amount in the v2
 exact scheme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The exact scheme only rejected an authorization below the required amount
(assert_enough_value). A payload authorizing more, e.g. 5000 for a 1000
requirement, verified and settled 5000: the payer was charged more than the
resource costs.

x402 v2 §9 defines invalid_exact_evm_payload_authorization_value_mismatch as
"Payment amount does not exactly match the required amount", and the TS
reference facilitator compares with !==. The v2 exact EIP-3009 and Permit2
paths now use assert_exact_value, which rejects any difference; the v2 exact
handler reports it as invalid_exact_evm_payload_authorization_value_mismatch.
The upto scheme, where the amount is a maximum, and v1 are unchanged.
